WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.240
Okay.

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:06.680
So we've been talking about with the virus,
should we be voting by mail in November?

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.200
And Donald Trump has insisted that vote by
mail leads to voter fraud, despite the fact

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.679
that he votes by mail.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:18.410
We've talked about really it's the swing states,
the battlegrounds that are most important

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.910
to ensure we can vote by mail so that we don't
hold down Democratic turnout, you know, vote

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.910
by mail or not.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.220
California's going to Joe Biden.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.220
Vote by mail or not.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.589
Massachusetts is going to Joe Biden.

00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:32.770
But it's those key swing states and even some
battleground or purplish red states where

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:36.210
it's really important that voting by mail
be done.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.930
We know that higher turnout is bad for Republicans
and we have really, really good news.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:47.000
Texas federal judge has ruled yesterday that
anyone who doesn't want to go out and vote

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.920
in person in Texas because they are afraid
of catching Corona virus is entitled to get

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.100
an absentee ballot.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.640
Now, this is not as good as vote by mail,
by default.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.840
And I'll explain to you why.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:03.350
The best scenario would be the state says
every registered voter is going to get an

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.789
absentee ballot in the mail, whether they
request one or not.

00:01:06.789 --> 00:01:09.759
This is not that you do have to request an
absentee ballot.

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:15.750
But in normal circumstances in Texas, you
have to justify why are you asking for an

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.750
absentee ballot?

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.020
You have to meet certain criteria.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.890
And it would be a fight over.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:26.679
Does fear of catching the virus qualify, qualify
you for an absentee ballot?

00:01:26.679 --> 00:01:33.200
We've now heard from District Judge Fred Berhe
and Judge Fred Beary says the disability provision

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:39.140
applies to any voter who does not have immunity
to Corona virus and fears they would catch

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.200
it at a polling place.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.299
This is a very technical ruling.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:48.280
Texas has this election code which defines
a disability as a sickness or physical condition

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.409
that prevents the voter from appearing at
the polling place on Election Day without

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:57.299
a likelihood of needing personal assistance
or of injuring the voter's health.

00:01:57.299 --> 00:02:04.650
The court said fear and anxiety is inextricably
intertwined with voters physical health.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:10.990
And if you are apprehensive about going to
the vote, going to the in-person ballot box

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:15.900
and catching Corona virus, that is a limit
on your ability to cast a ballot.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:22.000
So the court decided lack of immunity to the
right to the coronavirus counts as a physical

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
condition.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.430
You would be entitled to request an absentee
ballot under that pretense.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.470
Now, there's a few caveats here.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:34.501
You will be able to do this request an absentee
ballot merely for fear of catching corona

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:40.640
virus until this decision goes to trial or
the pandemic goes away.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.530
So I don't know how you define the pandemic
has gone away in November.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:50.740
If there are fewer cases, if there are fewer
deaths, would that potentially be seen as

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.690
there is no more pandemic and voters will
not be allowed to vote for president by mail?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:03:00.330
Right now, this will apply to the July elections
in Texas, for example, July 14th.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.880
There's a primary runoff in Texas.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.090
Anybody who is afraid of catching Corona virus
will be able to request an absentee ballot.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.620
November is still more of a question mark.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.780
And, of course, Republicans still don't like
it.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.120
They're going to fight to have this canceled.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.600
By the time of the presidential election,
you've got the Texas attorney general, Ken

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:21.680
Paxton, who says that this could be something
that opens the door to fraud.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.990
And this is the talking point that the right
is choosing to die on.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.140
Essentially, it's the hill they're choosing
to die on.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.760
Voting by mail should be available to anybody
who wants it.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:32.760
Period.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.050
The entire state of Oregon has had vote by
mail for 20 years, more than 20 years.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:38.650
They've put it in place in 1998.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.820
They had a ballot initiative.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.930
It passed about 70 to 30.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:47.370
And it's funny how you look at the arguments
in 1998 against vote 97, 98 against vote by

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.970
mail in Oregon.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:52.000
And it's the exact same thing that Republicans
are saying right now.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.320
You go back and look at the comments in the
90s in Oregon from people like state Rep.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:02.320
Lynn Snodgrass or anti-tax activist Bill Sizemore
in the 90s.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.700
They were saying we can't have vote by mail
in Oregon.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.850
It'll invite election fraud.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.620
It'll allow people to pressure others about
how they vote.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.940
Now, the truth is, vote by mail is very popular
in Oregon.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.680
Eighty one percent support in 2003.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.650
Really hard to get 80 percent support for
anything right now.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:27.319
But more importantly, 30 percent of respondents
in Oregon in 2003 said they vote more often

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:30.150
since vote by mail was an active enacted.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.430
That is what Republicans don't want.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:36.270
That is what scares the hell out of Trump
about vote by mail for November of twenty

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.270
twenty.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:42.819
Let's put a vote by mail in place in more
places.

00:04:42.819 --> 00:04:45.840
And let's also understand that we should really
focus in on the swing states.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.770
Now, on the fraud question, vote by mail does
not lead to more fraud.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.910
Check out the numbers that we have.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:05:01.350
Over the last 20 years, 250 million votes
have been cast by mail nationally.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:07.069
Twelve hundred cases of voter fraud in all
forms have been identified.

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:09.289
Eleven hundred resulting in criminal convictions.

00:05:09.289 --> 00:05:11.740
So what do we know over the last 20 years?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.379
We have had almost no actual voter fraud.

00:05:16.379 --> 00:05:20.520
It almost always eleven hundred out of twelve
hundred times.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.749
It led to a criminal conviction, meaning you
are very likely to get punished and be found

00:05:24.749 --> 00:05:29.110
guilty if you participate in voter fraud.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:35.139
And when you look at how many of those were
with absentee ballots, it's only 200 of the

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:36.139
12 hundred.

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:39.410
OK, so of the almost non-existent voter fraud.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:44.669
Twelve hundred cases, one sixth were with
absentee ballots.

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:48.319
That means seven or eight cases per year nationally.

00:05:48.319 --> 00:05:49.400
OK.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.400
Seven or eight?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.240
Not seven or eight percent.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.440
Not point seven point eight percent.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.979
Seven or eight cases nationally per year of.

00:05:57.979 --> 00:06:01.879
Absentee ballot related voter fraud, which
is only one sixth of the total.

00:06:01.879 --> 00:06:03.540
Most of them are in-person.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.800
No methodology is perfect.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.499
Fraud is not an issue with vote by mail.

00:06:08.499 --> 00:06:10.559
Do not let them trick you.

00:06:10.559 --> 00:06:13.879
Make them provide the evidence of it because
there is no evidence.

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:13.979
The numbers are overwhelming

